## 32. Important Indian Regulations

### Labour Codes

India's four Labour Codes came into effect on 21 November 2025.

They include provisions relating to wages, worker protection, employment conditions and social security, including gig and platform workers.

The National Social Security Board for Unorganised Workers and Gig & Platform Workers was notified on 30 October 2026.

ZEVRO must review the applicable central and Karnataka rules and schemes before launch.

Sources:
https://www.labour.gov.in/
https://www.pib.gov.in/

### Data Protection

India's Digital Personal Data Protection Rules were notified on 14 November 2025.

ZEVRO will handle personal information belonging to customers, workers and business representatives.

It should establish:

- Privacy policy.
- Appropriate consent mechanisms.
- Purpose limitation.
- Data retention rules.
- Security safeguards.
- User-rights processes.
- Data breach response.

Source:
https://www.meity.gov.in/

### GST

ZEVRO must determine its GST obligations based on its exact operating model.

Section 52 of the CGST Act contains Tax Collection at Source requirements for applicable electronic commerce operators.

The precise applicability depends on the transactions and contractual structure.

Source:
https://cbic-gst.gov.in/

### Digital Payments

Use an appropriately authorised payment service provider.

RBI's Payment Aggregator Master Direction was updated on 11 November 2026.

Source:
https://www.rbi.org.in/

### Other Areas

- Company registration.
- Business agreements.
- Worker classification.
- Applicable minimum wages.
- Payroll and statutory contributions.
- Insurance.
