# PART 18 – RISKS AND CHALLENGES

## 37. What Can Go Wrong?

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Low worker availability | Recruit before opening customer demand |
| Unreliable service providers | Verification and quality monitoring |
| Worker no-shows | Availability confirmation and backup supply |
| Customer complaints | Transparent support and dispute policies |
| Payment delays | Proper contracts and payment controls |
| High acquisition costs | Local partnerships and repeat customers |
| Business non-payment | Credit controls and written contracts |
| High operational complexity | Start with limited categories |
| Legal issues | Professional compliance review |
| Strong competitors | Differentiated service and execution |
| Poor worker retention | Transparent pay and respectful worker policies |

## 38. Important Startup Challenges

ZEVRO is a two-sided or multi-sided marketplace.

It must acquire customers and workers at the same time.

For B2B, it must also establish trust with businesses and consistently fulfil workforce requirements.

The biggest challenge will not be developing the app.

It will be ensuring that the right worker is available at the right time, completes the work and receives the correct payment.

That should be ZEVRO's operational priority.

