# PART 20 – DEVELOPMENT ROADMAP

## 40. First 90 Days

### Days 1–30: Validate the Business

- Interview potential business customers.
- Interview workers.
- Identify operational requirements.
- Select one initial category.
- Understand customer pricing expectations.
- Identify legal responsibilities.
- Obtain pilot commitments.

Suggested research targets:

- 20–30 business interviews.
- 40–50 worker interviews.
- 15–20 customer interviews where B2C is being evaluated.

These are proposed research targets, not existing customer numbers.

### Days 31–60: Build the MVP

Develop:

- Worker registration.
- Business registration.
- Worker profiles.
- Job posting.
- Applications.
- Matching.
- Shift allocation.
- Attendance.
- Admin management.
- Basic payment tracking.

The initial pilot can use manual operations where necessary.

### Days 61–90: Pilot Launch

- Onboard the first worker group.
- Work with initial business customers.
- Process actual workforce requirements.
- Measure fulfilment.
- Track worker payment accuracy.
- Collect feedback.
- Improve the platform.

### Suggested Pilot Success Gates

These are internal targets to test, not industry benchmarks:

- At least two recurring business customers.
- Consistent fulfilment of posted requirements.
- At least 90% attendance among confirmed workers.
- Clear payment reconciliation.
- Low complaint rates.
- Evidence of repeat business demand.

Do not expand until the pilot shows repeatability.

